@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:security] trusted-review-controller
Secret-bearing review jobs MUST execute only the trusted base controller and pinned review tools.
PR source is review data: it MUST NOT be installed, tested or run with provider credentials or a
write-capable GitHub token. The model runs read-only as an unprivileged user.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] advisory-review-result
Review status MUST identify the exact reviewed head and base. Missing, malformed, stale or
incomplete output MUST NOT be reported as a completed review. Findings MUST remain advisory;
agents MAY resolve false positives with an explanation. A completed review is not semantic approval.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] complete-python-ci
Python CI groups MUST cover normal active pytest collection exactly once. Retired experiment suites
MUST remain excluded from collection and CI (owner 2026-11-07); exclusion MUST NOT be reported as a pass.
Shared tooling and active game coverage MUST remain enabled. While macOS CI is
deferred (owner 2026-10-23, TASKS MAC1) the macOS-only board group is disabled and its coverage is
deferred, not passed. The aggregate merge check MUST fail when any enabled group fails, is cancelled
or is skipped. Re-enabling macOS CI (MAC1) MUST restore the board group to the aggregate. Cached
Rust artifacts MUST NOT hide a failed compile: CI MUST remove the board crate's artifacts and
successfully rebuild it before testing.
Only successful board jobs on main MAY publish the shared Rust cache; PRs only restore it.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] explicit-paid-review-request
Paid contract review MUST start only from a newly created exact `r? cc` comment by an authorized writer
account, never from a PR open/push event. Missing-request notices MUST remain advisory and cost no
provider calls. Documentation-only and writer-declared exact-head trivial changes MUST be exempt
from the request rule and warning; a declaration MUST NOT carry over to a new head.
